---@class posthog.experiments.CreateExperimentsCalculateRunningTimeRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field metric_type posthog.experiments.MetricTypeEnum|string Metric type to size for. 'funnel' for conversion rates, 'mean_count' for event counts per user, 'mean_sum_or_avg' for summed property values per user, 'ratio' and 'retention' for ratio-style metrics (both require baseline_stats or an explicit variance). * `funnel` - funnel * `mean_count` - mean_count * `mean_sum_or_avg` - mean_sum_or_avg * `ratio` - ratio * `retention` - retention
---@field minimum_detectable_effect number Smallest relative change to detect, as a percentage (e.g. 5 means a 5% lift). Must be > 0.
---@field number_of_variants? number Total number of variants including control (default 2, at most 100).
---@field exposure_rate_per_day? number|distilled.Null Expected exposures per day. When provided, the response includes the recommended running time.
---@field baseline_value? number|distilled.Null Baseline metric value: conversion rate as a fraction 0-1 (funnel), average per user (mean), or the ratio (ratio/retention). Provide this or baseline_stats.
---@field variance? number|distilled.Null Pre-computed variance per user. Provide this or baseline_stats when metric_type is ratio/retention and baseline_value is given directly. When given, it replaces the variance the calculator derives for any metric type, including p(1-p) for funnels.
---@field baseline_stats? posthog.experiments.RunningTimeBaselineStats|distilled.Null Raw control-group statistics. When provided, the server derives baseline_value and variance.

---@class posthog.experiments.CreateExperimentsEndRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id number A unique integer value identifying this experiment.
---@field conclusion? posthog.experiments.ConclusionEnum|string|distilled.Null The conclusion of the experiment. * `won` - won * `lost` - lost * `inconclusive` - inconclusive * `stopped_early` - stopped_early * `invalid` - invalid
---@field conclusion_comment? string|distilled.Null Optional comment about the experiment conclusion.
---@field open_cleanup_pr? boolean When true, open a draft pull request that removes the experiment's feature-flag code from the linked repository. A personal API key needs the task:write scope (403 otherwise). Skipped when the conclusion is empty, or when no connected repository can be resolved.
---@field repository? string|distilled.Null GitHub repository to open the cleanup pull request in, in `organization/repository` format. Only used when open_cleanup_pr is true. It must be one of the team's connected repositories (see the flag_cleanup_target action); it is then saved as the experiment's repository. When omitted, the experiment's saved repository, the team's default cleanup repository, or the team's only connected repository is used.
---@field set_repository_as_team_default? boolean When true, also save `repository` as this environment's default cleanup repository, used for experiments that have no repository of their own. Only acts when open_cleanup_pr is true and `repository` is provided and belongs to the team's GitHub installation. Requires project admin access (403 otherwise).

