---@class posthog.experiments.CreateExperimentsSetupContextRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field target_event? string|distilled.Null Event that marks a visit to the surface under test, for example '$pageview' or '$screen'. Needed for target_surface and for the baseline in candidate_metric.
---@field target_url_contains? string|distilled.Null Only counts target events whose $current_url contains this text, ignoring case. Needs target_event to be '$pageview'.
---@field target_properties? posthog.experiments.ExperimentSetupPropertyFilterList|distilled.Null Event or person property filters that narrow the target event, for example an exact $host and $pathname for one page. At most 10 filters, and each needs type 'event' or 'person'. Needs target_event. Combines with target_url_contains.
---@field metric_event? string|distilled.Null Event of the candidate primary metric. With target_event, candidate_metric returns a baseline. Without it, candidate_metric returns only the event's volume. Also marks the shared metrics that count this event.
---@field metric_properties? posthog.experiments.ExperimentSetupPropertyFilterList|distilled.Null Event or person property filters that narrow the metric event, for the metric that counts only some of its occurrences. At most 10 filters, and each needs type 'event' or 'person'. Needs metric_event.
---@field previous_experiments_limit? number How many experiments to return, most recently launched first, then drafts, 1 to 25.
---@field shared_metrics_limit? number How many shared metrics to return, most reused first, 1 to 25.

---@class posthog.experiments.CreateExperimentsShipVariantRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id number A unique integer value identifying this experiment.
---@field conclusion? posthog.experiments.ConclusionEnum|string|distilled.Null The conclusion of the experiment. * `won` - won * `lost` - lost * `inconclusive` - inconclusive * `stopped_early` - stopped_early * `invalid` - invalid
---@field conclusion_comment? string|distilled.Null Optional comment about the experiment conclusion.
---@field open_cleanup_pr? boolean When true, open a draft pull request that removes the experiment's feature-flag code from the linked repository. A personal API key needs the task:write scope (403 otherwise). Skipped when the conclusion is empty, or when no connected repository can be resolved.
---@field repository? string|distilled.Null GitHub repository to open the cleanup pull request in, in `organization/repository` format. Only used when open_cleanup_pr is true. It must be one of the team's connected repositories (see the flag_cleanup_target action); it is then saved as the experiment's repository. When omitted, the experiment's saved repository, the team's default cleanup repository, or the team's only connected repository is used.
---@field set_repository_as_team_default? boolean When true, also save `repository` as this environment's default cleanup repository, used for experiments that have no repository of their own. Only acts when open_cleanup_pr is true and `repository` is provided and belongs to the team's GitHub installation. Requires project admin access (403 otherwise).
---@field variant_key? string The key of the variant to ship.
---@field release_to_everyone? boolean If true, prepend a release condition to the feature flag that rolls the variant out to 100% of users, overriding any existing release conditions on the flag. If false (default), only update the variant distribution — existing release conditions are preserved and the variant is served only to users who already match them.

