---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckResult
---@field key posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckKeyEnum Stable identifier of the check. A check can report several finding codes, so the key is not a finding code. * `flag_state` - Flag State * `flag_shared` - Flag Shared * `flag_history` - Flag History * `split_changed_mid_run` - Split Changed Mid Run * `bucketing_changed_mid_run` - Bucketing Changed Mid Run * `release_conditions_changed_mid_run` - Release Conditions Changed Mid Run * `flag_variants_mismatch` - Flag Variants Mismatch * `forced_variant_release_condition` - Forced Variant Release Condition * `new_flag_no_traffic` - New Flag No Traffic * `no_metric` - No Metric * `metric_event_not_ingested` - Metric Event Not Ingested * `metric_cannot_compile` - Metric Cannot Compile * `metric_calculation_failed` - Metric Calculation Failed * `metric_all_zero` - Metric All Zero * `exposure_criteria_cannot_match` - Exposure Criteria Cannot Match * `exposure_filters` - Exposure Filters * `early_significance` - Early Significance * `metrics_not_matured` - Metrics Not Matured * `zero_exposures` - Zero Exposures * `test_account_filter_removes_exposures` - Test Account Filter Removes Exposures * `srm` - Srm * `bias_risk_multiple_excluded` - Bias Risk Multiple Excluded * `multiple_variants_share` - Multiple Variants Share
---@field name string The problem the check looks for, for example 'Metrics not set up'.
---@field description string What the check looks for and why it matters. The same for every experiment and every status.
---@field status posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckStatusEnum passed: the check found no problem. finding: the check reported a finding in `findings`. not_applicable: the check does not cover the experiment's current state, for example a check of the changes since launch on a draft. not_checked: the check covers the experiment, but it could not read an input or it failed, so a problem it looks for can be present without a finding. * `passed` - Passed * `finding` - Finding * `not_applicable` - Not Applicable * `not_checked` - Not Checked
---@field reason string|distilled.Null Why the check did not look, for the statuses not_applicable and not_checked, for example 'Runs after launch'. Null for passed and finding.
---@field values posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckResultValuesMap What the check read on the experiment, for every status, as numbers, strings, booleans or null. Empty when the check read nothing or shows nothing. The suffix of a key gives the unit: _count is a count, _percentage is on the 0-100 scale, _hours is hours and _at is an ISO 8601 time in UTC. A key without a suffix is a setting or a state. A key means the same thing in every check. `rule.value` names the key that decides.
---@field rule posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckRule|distilled.Null How the check decides. The same for every experiment and every status. Null for a check without a numeric rule.

---What the check read on the experiment, for every status, as numbers, strings, booleans or null. Empty when the check read nothing or shows nothing. The suffix of a key gives the unit: _count is a count, _percentage is on the 0-100 scale, _hours is hours and _at is an ISO 8601 time in UTC. A key without a suffix is a setting or a state. A key means the same thing in every check. `rule.value` names the key that decides.
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckResultValuesMap { [string]: posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckResultValuesValue|distilled.Null }

---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckResultValuesValue string|number|boolean

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckRule
---@field value posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthValueKeyEnum The key in `values` that the check compares with the threshold. * `exposed_count` - Users or groups exposed since launch, as the exposure criteria count them, including those exposed to multiple variants * `compared_count` - Exposed users or groups in the variants that the sample ratio test compares, without those exposed to multiple variants * `multiple_variant_count` - Users or groups exposed to more than one variant * `multiple_variant_percentage` - multiple_variant_count as a share of exposed_count * `multiple_variant_handling` - What the results do with users exposed to more than one variant: exclude or first_seen * `p_value` - P-value of the sample ratio test * `since_launch_hours` - Hours since launch * `exposed_without_test_account_filter_count` - Users or groups that the exposure criteria count without the test account filters * `kept_by_test_account_filter_percentage` - exposed_count as a share of exposed_without_test_account_filter_count * `only_count_matured_users` - Whether "Require completed conversion or retention window" is on * `primary_metric_count` - Primary metrics that the calculation computes * `waiting_metric_count` - Of the primary metrics, those whose conversion or retention window hasn't passed for any user yet * `metric_count` - Metrics that the calculation computes * `completed_metric_count` - Metrics whose result of the latest calculation the page shows * `failed_metric_count` - Metrics whose latest calculation failed * `calculated_at` - When the latest calculation of the metrics finished * `flag_active` - Whether the feature flag is enabled * `flag_deleted` - Whether the feature flag is deleted * `flag_rolled_out` - Whether a release condition of the feature flag rolls out to more than 0% * `shipped_variant` - The key of the variant that the feature flag serves to everyone, or null when it serves more than one
---@field threshold number The threshold, in the unit that the suffix of the key gives.
---@field warns posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthRuleSideEnum above: the check reports a finding when the value is above the threshold. below: when the value is below it. A value at the threshold passes. * `above` - Finding above the threshold * `below` - Finding below the threshold
---@field test posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthRuleTestEnum|distilled.Null The statistical test that computes the value, for example chi_squared. Null for a count or a share. * `chi_squared` - Chi-squared goodness-of-fit test
---@field minimum posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthRuleMinimum|distilled.Null What the check needs before it judges. Null when the check judges from the first value.

---* `passed` - Passed
---* `finding` - Finding
---* `not_applicable` - Not Applicable
---* `not_checked` - Not Checked
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckStatusEnum "passed"|"finding"|"not_applicable"|"not_checked"

---The result of each health check, in the order the checks run. The checks that read the exposure counts are not here: the exposure query returns them as `health_checks`.
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthChecksList posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckResult[]

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthFinding
---@field code posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthFindingCodeEnum Stable identifier of the problem. Each code has one meaning across every surface that reports it. * `flag_off_while_running` - Flag Off While Running * `variant_shipped_while_running` - Variant Shipped While Running * `flag_live_after_end` - Flag Live After End * `flag_live_before_launch` - Flag Live Before Launch * `bias_risk_multiple_excluded` - Bias Risk Multiple Excluded * `multiple_variants_share` - Multiple Variants Share * `no_metric` - No Metric * `metric_event_not_ingested` - Metric Event Not Ingested * `metric_cannot_compile` - Metric Cannot Compile * `metric_calculation_failed` - Metric Calculation Failed * `metric_all_zero` - Metric All Zero * `exposure_criteria_cannot_match` - Exposure Criteria Cannot Match * `exposure_filter_on_dynamic_cohort` - Exposure Filter On Dynamic Cohort * `srm` - Sample Ratio Mismatch * `zero_exposures` - Zero Exposures * `test_account_filter_removes_exposures` - Test Account Filter Removes Exposures * `forced_variant_release_condition` - Forced Variant Release Condition * `flag_variants_mismatch` - Flag Variants Mismatch * `split_changed_mid_run` - Split Changed Mid Run * `bucketing_changed_mid_run` - Bucketing Changed Mid Run * `release_conditions_changed_mid_run` - Release Conditions Changed Mid Run * `new_flag_no_traffic` - New Flag No Traffic * `early_significance` - Early Significance * `metrics_not_matured` - Metrics Not Matured * `flag_shared` - Flag Shared
---@field subcode string|distilled.Null The case within the code, when a code covers several, for example 'running_but_no_rollout' within 'flag_off_while_running'. Null when the code has one case.
---@field reason string|distilled.Null A stable qualifier below the subcode: where a sample ratio mismatch is located ('library', 'page'), what leaves nobody exposed ('test_account_filter'), what made a metric reach a query limit ('metric', 'exposure_criteria'), or why a check could not read what it needs ('no_history_access'). Null when the finding names none.
---@field severity posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthFindingSeverityEnum How much the problem affects the results: critical, warning, or info. * `critical` - Critical severity * `warning` - Warning severity * `info` - Info severity
---@field title string One-line summary of the problem.
---@field detail string What is wrong, what it does to the experiment, and how to fix it.
---@field evidence posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthFindingEvidenceMap The values behind the finding, such as the key of a shipped variant or the share of users exposed to multiple variants. The keys depend on the code.
---@field actions posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthFindingActionsList The actions that fix the problem, in order of preference, for example 'open_feature_flag' or 'add_primary_metric'.
---@field diagnostic_ref string|distilled.Null The id of the matching diagnostic in the diagnosing-experiment-health skill, for example 'A5'. Null when the skill has none.
---@field check posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthCheckKeyEnum The key of the check in `checks` that reported the finding. A check can report several codes, so the code doesn't name the check. * `flag_state` - Flag State * `flag_shared` - Flag Shared * `flag_history` - Flag History * `split_changed_mid_run` - Split Changed Mid Run * `bucketing_changed_mid_run` - Bucketing Changed Mid Run * `release_conditions_changed_mid_run` - Release Conditions Changed Mid Run * `flag_variants_mismatch` - Flag Variants Mismatch * `forced_variant_release_condition` - Forced Variant Release Condition * `new_flag_no_traffic` - New Flag No Traffic * `no_metric` - No Metric * `metric_event_not_ingested` - Metric Event Not Ingested * `metric_cannot_compile` - Metric Cannot Compile * `metric_calculation_failed` - Metric Calculation Failed * `metric_all_zero` - Metric All Zero * `exposure_criteria_cannot_match` - Exposure Criteria Cannot Match * `exposure_filters` - Exposure Filters * `early_significance` - Early Significance * `metrics_not_matured` - Metrics Not Matured * `zero_exposures` - Zero Exposures * `test_account_filter_removes_exposures` - Test Account Filter Removes Exposures * `srm` - Srm * `bias_risk_multiple_excluded` - Bias Risk Multiple Excluded * `multiple_variants_share` - Multiple Variants Share

