---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputs
---@field is_launched boolean Whether the experiment has a start date.
---@field is_running boolean Whether the experiment is launched and not ended.
---@field has_ended boolean Whether the experiment has an end date.
---@field is_paused boolean Whether the experiment is paused.
---@field archived boolean Whether the experiment is archived.
---@field baseline_variant_key string|distilled.Null The baseline set in the experiment's settings. Null when unset.
---@field excluded_variant_keys posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExcludedVariantKeysList The variants the analysis leaves out of the results. The forced-variant check ignores pins to them.
---@field primary_metric_count number Single-use primary metrics plus shared metrics linked as primary.
---@field secondary_metric_count number Single-use secondary metrics plus shared metrics linked as secondary.
---@field flag posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlag|distilled.Null The experiment's feature flag. Null when it has none.
---@field flag_last_called_at string|distilled.Null The flag's latest recorded call, which a periodic sync of the flag call events sets. Null when the experiment has no flag, or the flag has no recorded call.
---@field flag_called boolean|distilled.Null Whether PostHog has recorded any call of the flag. The flag traffic check reads it on a draft. Null when the experiment has no flag, or the organization's flag calls are stored where the checks can't read them.
---@field flag_called_during_run boolean|distilled.Null Whether PostHog has recorded a call of the flag between launch and the end, or until now. The zero exposures check reads it to say whether the flag is called. Null before launch, after a latest call that came after the end, or when the organization's flag calls can't be read.
---@field flag_called_after_end boolean|distilled.Null Whether PostHog has recorded a call of the flag after the end and within the last 3 days. The flag state check reads it on an ended experiment whose flag is still active with multiple variants. False only once 3 days have passed since the end. Null before the end, before those 3 days are over without a call, or when the organization's flag calls can't be read.
---@field exposure_events posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposureEvents|distilled.Null The events the exposure criteria count. Null when the stored exposure criteria don't parse.
---@field events_received posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsEventsReceivedMap Whether the project has received each event that the metrics and the exposure criteria name, by event name. A name that ingestion keeps no record of is absent.
---@field metric_compiles posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsMetricCompiles|distilled.Null The compile of each metric's query without running it, as the reader, which the 'Invalid metric definitions' check reads. A metric that compiles is cached per reader for a day, and a failing metric compiles again on every request. Null when the compile itself failed.
---@field latest_calculation posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsLatestCalculation|distilled.Null The latest finished calculation of the metrics, which the metric results check reads. Null before launch, on an archived experiment, or when the read failed.
---@field flag_history posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlagHistory|distilled.Null The changes of the flag since launch that can move exposed people. Null when the experiment is not running, is archived, its flag is missing or deleted, or the read failed.
---@field condition_set_traffic_status posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsTrafficStatusEnum Whether the condition-set traffic was read, or why not. The forced-variant check needs it when the experiment is launched and some but not all release conditions pin a variant that has a share of the split and is not excluded from the analysis. The release-condition check needs it when such an override was removed after launch. * `read` - Read * `not_needed` - Not Needed * `no_query_access` - No Query Access * `denied_properties` - Denied Properties * `no_flag_version` - No Flag Version * `unknown` - Unknown
---@field condition_set_traffic posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsConditionSetTraffic|distilled.Null The flag's recent calls by condition set. Null unless condition_set_traffic_status is 'read'.
---@field reader_access posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsReaderAccess What the reader may read, which decides what the checks can load.
---@field exposures posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposures The exposure query's answer that the exposure checks read, from the cache.
---@field project posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsProject Facts about the project that no check reads yet, from the same providers as the setup context.

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsConditionSetPeople
---@field condition_set number The number of the release condition, from 1.
---@field people number The people whose latest call this condition served.

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsConditionSetTraffic
---@field since string The start of the window: the latest of launch, the flag's last save and 7 days ago.
---@field team_timezone string The project's time zone, which the finding uses for times.
---@field people_by_set posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsConditionSetTrafficPeopleBySetList People by the release condition that served their latest call of the flag's version.
---@field calls number The flag's calls in the window, of any flag version.
---@field remotely_evaluated_calls number The calls that the flag service evaluated. Only those name a condition set. Local evaluation in a server SDK and a bootstrapped value name none.
---@field people_assigned_outside number The people who got a variant from a call without a flag version that is no local evaluation in a server SDK, from an hour after the start of the window: a bootstrap or the caller's own assignment. With a 0% rollout, 10 or more of them turn `running_but_no_rollout` into `assigned_outside_flag_service`.

---People by the release condition that served their latest call of the flag's version.
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsConditionSetTrafficPeopleBySetList posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsConditionSetPeople[]

---Whether the project has received each event that the metrics and the exposure criteria name, by event name. A name that ingestion keeps no record of is absent.
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsEventsReceivedMap { [string]: boolean }

---The variants the analysis leaves out of the results. The forced-variant check ignores pins to them.
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExcludedVariantKeysList string[]

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposedBetween
---@field kind posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthFlagChangeKindEnum The kind of change. A bucketing change is a change of a setting that decides the variant draw. * `split` - Split * `bucketing` - Bucketing * `release_conditions` - Release-condition
---@field question string What was asked, as the staff view names it.
---@field exposed boolean|distilled.Null Whether anyone was exposed between the first and the last counted change of this kind. Asked only when the last sets back what the first changed. Null when not asked or unknown.

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposureEvents
---@field custom_event string|distilled.Null The event the exposure criteria count in place of the flag calls. Null for flag calls or an action.
---@field required_flag_key string|distilled.Null The flag key the exposure query requires on the flag call events. Null for a custom event or an action.
---@field variant_property string The event property that holds the variant.
---@field activation string|distilled.Null The event, or the action's name, that has to follow a user's flag call before the user counts. Null without an activation.

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposureTotals
---@field total_exposures posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposureTotalsTotalExposuresMap Exposed people by variant. '$multiple' counts the people exposed to more than one variant.
---@field multiple_variant_handling string How the analysis treats people in several variants: 'exclude' or 'first_seen'.
---@field sample_ratio_mismatch_p_value number|distilled.Null The p-value of the sample ratio test. Null when there was too little data.
---@field hours_since_launch number|distilled.Null Hours from launch to the computation of the answer, as the checks read them.

---Exposed people by variant. '$multiple' counts the people exposed to more than one variant.
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposureTotalsTotalExposuresMap { [string]: number }

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposures
---@field status posthog.experiments.HealthExposureInputsStatusEnum Whether a cached answer was read. 'calculating' means no answer is cached and a calculation runs in the background, so a later request reads a fresh answer. 'stale' means the cached answer is past its age: a recalculation runs in the background, or the last one failed and 'error' says why. After a failed calculation, no new one starts for 20 minutes. * `ready` - Ready * `stale` - Stale * `calculating` - Calculating * `not_launched` - Not Launched * `no_query_access` - No Query Access * `failed` - Failed
---@field computed_at string|distilled.Null When the answer was computed.
---@field totals posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposureTotals|distilled.Null What the exposure checks read. Null without an answer.
---@field findings posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposuresFindingsList The findings of the exposure checks on this answer: zero exposures, SRM and bias risk.
---@field error string|distilled.Null Why the query or its last background calculation failed. Set for 'failed', and for 'stale' when the recalculation failed.

---The findings of the exposure checks on this answer: zero exposures, SRM and bias risk.
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsExposuresFindingsList posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthFinding[]

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlag
---@field active boolean Whether the flag is enabled.
---@field deleted boolean Whether the flag is deleted.
---@field release_conditions posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlagReleaseConditionsList The flag's release conditions, in evaluation order.
---@field variants posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlagVariantsList The flag's variants and their split.
---@field split_text string The split as text, in the form of a change's before and after, such as 'control 50%, test 50%'.

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlagChange
---@field kind posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthFlagChangeKindEnum The kind of change. A bucketing change is a change of a setting that decides the variant draw. * `split` - Split * `bucketing` - Bucketing * `release_conditions` - Release-condition
---@field changed_at string When the flag changed.
---@field changed string What changed, as the staff view names it, such as 'Split' or 'Key'.
---@field before string The value before the change as text, such as 'control 50%, test 50%' or 'device_id'. 'none' when unset.
---@field after string The value after the change, in the same form.
---@field counted boolean Whether the checks count this change: every change counts from the first change, of any kind, with an exposure before it, or an unknown answer. False for every change when not checked.

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlagHistory
---@field checked boolean Whether the changes were compared with the exposures. False when not_checked_reason is set.
---@field not_checked_reason string|distilled.Null Why the changes were not compared with the exposures: 'no_history_access', 'no_query_access', 'exposure_filters', 'exposure_action' or 'exposure_criteria'. Null when they were.
---@field start_date string The experiment's start date. The flag history counts changes from it, as the results count exposures from it.
---@field team_timezone string The project's time zone, which the findings use for times.
---@field changes posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlagHistoryChangesList Every change since launch that can move exposed people, of every kind, in time order. A bucketing change is one per setting and save. A rollout change alone is no release-condition change. Empty for 'no_history_access', which does not read them.
---@field exposed_before_first boolean|distilled.Null Whether anyone was exposed before the first counted change. Null when unknown or not checked.
---@field exposed_between posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlagHistoryExposedBetweenList One entry for each kind of change with a counted change, in the order of the kinds.

---Every change since launch that can move exposed people, of every kind, in time order. A bucketing change is one per setting and save. A rollout change alone is no release-condition change. Empty for 'no_history_access', which does not read them.
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlagHistoryChangesList posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthInputsFlagChange[]

