---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthReleaseCondition
---@field rollout_percentage number The share of the users matching the condition set's filters who get the flag, from 0 to 100.
---@field property_count number The number of filters a user must match, such as properties and cohorts. 0 matches all users.
---@field aggregation_group_type_index number|distilled.Null The group type the condition set assigns variants by: its own, or the flag's when it sets none. Null when it assigns them by user.

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthRuleMinimum
---@field value posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthValueKeyEnum The key in `values` that must reach the threshold before the check judges. * `exposed_count` - Users or groups exposed since launch, as the exposure criteria count them, including those exposed to multiple variants * `compared_count` - Exposed users or groups in the variants that the sample ratio test compares, without those exposed to multiple variants * `multiple_variant_count` - Users or groups exposed to more than one variant * `multiple_variant_percentage` - multiple_variant_count as a share of exposed_count * `multiple_variant_handling` - What the results do with users exposed to more than one variant: exclude or first_seen * `p_value` - P-value of the sample ratio test * `since_launch_hours` - Hours since launch * `exposed_without_test_account_filter_count` - Users or groups that the exposure criteria count without the test account filters * `kept_by_test_account_filter_percentage` - exposed_count as a share of exposed_without_test_account_filter_count * `only_count_matured_users` - Whether "Require completed conversion or retention window" is on * `primary_metric_count` - Primary metrics that the calculation computes * `waiting_metric_count` - Of the primary metrics, those whose conversion or retention window hasn't passed for any user yet * `metric_count` - Metrics that the calculation computes * `completed_metric_count` - Metrics whose result of the latest calculation the page shows * `failed_metric_count` - Metrics whose latest calculation failed * `calculated_at` - When the latest calculation of the metrics finished * `flag_active` - Whether the feature flag is enabled * `flag_deleted` - Whether the feature flag is deleted * `flag_rolled_out` - Whether a release condition of the feature flag rolls out to more than 0% * `shipped_variant` - The key of the variant that the feature flag serves to everyone, or null when it serves more than one
---@field threshold number The value that the key must reach. Below it, the check reports no finding.

---* `above` - Finding above the threshold
---* `below` - Finding below the threshold
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthRuleSideEnum "above"|"below"

---* `chi_squared` - Chi-squared goodness-of-fit test
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthRuleTestEnum "chi_squared"

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthSetup
---@field release_conditions posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthSetupReleaseConditionsList The flag's condition sets as stored, in the order the flag evaluates them. Whether a set can serve a request depends on the sets before it and on `early_exit`.
---@field early_exit boolean Whether the flag stops at the first condition set whose filters match, also when its rollout leaves the user out. Otherwise such a user goes on to the next set.
---@field bucketing_identifier posthog.experiments.BucketingIdentifierEnum The flag's `bucketing_identifier`. Null on the flag reads as distinct_id. * `distinct_id` - User ID (default) * `device_id` - Device ID
---@field aggregation_group_type_index number|distilled.Null The flag's own group type, which the exposure counts and the results use. A condition set can override it. Null for users.
---@field evaluation_runtime posthog.experiments.EvaluationRuntimeEnum The flag's `evaluation_runtime`. Null on the flag reads as all. * `server` - Server * `client` - Client * `all` - All
---@field evaluation_contexts posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealthSetupEvaluationContextsList The names of the flag's evaluation contexts. When PostHog evaluates the flag, an SDK that sends evaluation contexts gets it only when it sends one of these, and an SDK that sends none gets it. Empty when the flag has none.
---@field ensure_experience_continuity boolean The flag's 'Persist flag across authentication steps' setting.

---The names of the flag's evaluation contexts. When PostHog evaluates the flag, an SDK that sends evaluation contexts gets it only when it sends one of these, and an SDK that sends none gets it. Empty when the flag has none.
