---A holdout group — a stable slice of users excluded from experiment exposure.
---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentHoldout
---@field id? number
---@field name? string Human-readable name for the holdout group.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Optional description of what this holdout reserves and why.
---@field filters? posthog.experiments.ExperimentHoldoutFiltersList Non-empty list of release-condition groups defining the held-out population, using the same shape as feature-flag release conditions. Each element's `rollout_percentage` (0–100, may be fractional) is the **exclusion** percentage — the share of users held back from all experiments that reference this holdout. `properties` optionally narrows the group by person/group properties. Do not set `variant`: the server normalizes it to `holdout-{id}`. Note that only the first element's `rollout_percentage` is embedded into each linked experiment's feature flag, and this population is shared across every experiment using the holdout.
---@field created_by? posthog.experiments.UserBasic|distilled.Null
---@field created_at? string
---@field updated_at? string
---@field user_access_level? string|distilled.Null The effective access level the user has for this object

