---POST response: the job just queued, or the one already active. It carries no results or live progress yet.
---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentMetricsRecalculationJob
---@field id string Unique identifier for this recalculation job
---@field experiment_id number ID of the experiment being recalculated
---@field status posthog.experiments.MetricsRecalculationStatusEnum Current status of the recalculation job * `pending` - Pending * `in_progress` - In Progress * `completed` - Completed * `failed` - Failed
---@field total_metrics number Total number of metrics to recalculate
---@field completed_metrics number Number of metrics with a COMPLETED result row in this run (derived, not stored)
---@field failed_metrics number Number of failed metrics in this run (derived): FAILED result rows plus discovery-step failures that never made it to a result row
---@field metric_errors any Terminal failure per metric_uuid: {step, message, error_type, retriable, timestamp, exposures_path}. retriable is true when a transient error exhausted its attempts, so a heal_latest_run or manual_retry can succeed; false when the metric config, the data, or a resource limit must change first. exposures_path is where the query read the exposures, and is missing when the query failed before it was built
---@field created_at string When the job was created
---@field started_at string|distilled.Null When processing started
---@field completed_at string|distilled.Null When processing completed
---@field query_to string|distilled.Null Upper time bound the metrics in this run were calculated against (the data freshness cutoff). Shared by every metric in the run; null until processing starts
---@field is_existing boolean True if returning an existing job rather than a newly created one

---GET latest: the newest terminal run, or the timeseries fallback, plus a pointer to any active run.
---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentMetricsRecalculationLatest
---@field id string Unique identifier for this recalculation job
---@field experiment_id number ID of the experiment being recalculated
---@field status posthog.experiments.MetricsRecalculationStatusEnum Current status of the recalculation job * `pending` - Pending * `in_progress` - In Progress * `completed` - Completed * `failed` - Failed
---@field total_metrics number Total number of metrics to recalculate
---@field completed_metrics number Number of metrics with a COMPLETED result row in this run (derived, not stored)
---@field failed_metrics number Number of failed metrics in this run (derived): FAILED result rows plus discovery-step failures that never made it to a result row
---@field metric_errors any Terminal failure per metric_uuid: {step, message, error_type, retriable, timestamp, exposures_path}. retriable is true when a transient error exhausted its attempts, so a heal_latest_run or manual_retry can succeed; false when the metric config, the data, or a resource limit must change first. exposures_path is where the query read the exposures, and is missing when the query failed before it was built
---@field created_at string When the job was created
---@field started_at string|distilled.Null When processing started
---@field completed_at string|distilled.Null When processing completed
---@field query_to string|distilled.Null Upper time bound the metrics in this run were calculated against (the data freshness cutoff). Shared by every metric in the run; null until processing starts
---@field metric_retries any Transient retry state per metric_uuid: {attempt, max_attempts, error_type, message, next_retry_at}. message is a user-safe description of the error that triggered the retry. Present only while a metric is between failed attempts; cleared when it succeeds or fails terminally, so treat entries for metrics that already have a result as stale.
---@field results posthog.experiments.ExperimentMetricsRecalculationLatestResultsList Per-metric results computed by this run, scoped by the run's recalc fingerprint
---@field rows_read? number|distilled.Null Rows read by the run's metric queries so far, both finished and currently running. Cumulative and roughly monotonic across the run; the primary live progress signal
---@field estimated_rows_total? number|distilled.Null ClickHouse's total_rows_approx across running queries plus the final read_rows of finished ones. A soft ceiling revised mid-scan, so it can exceed or trail rows_read; treat rows_read as the reliable signal
---@field active_run posthog.experiments.ActiveRecalculationRun|distilled.Null Run currently executing for this experiment, if any; poll it by id for live progress
---@field result_source posthog.experiments.ResultSourceEnum Where these results came from: 'recalculation' for a real metrics-recalculation run, 'timeseries_fallback' for a cold-start placeholder built from the latest daily timeseries data. * `recalculation` - recalculation * `timeseries_fallback` - timeseries_fallback

---Per-metric results computed by this run, scoped by the run's recalc fingerprint
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentMetricsRecalculationLatestResultsList posthog.experiments.MetricRecalculationResult[]

---* `manual` - Manual
---* `manual_retry` - Manual Retry
---* `cold_run` - Cold Run
---* `stale_refresh` - Stale Refresh
---* `heal_latest_run` - Heal Latest Run
---* `experiment_config_change` - Experiment Config Change
---* `metric_config_change` - Metric Config Change
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentMetricsRecalculationRequestTriggerEnum "manual"|"manual_retry"|"cold_run"|"stale_refresh"|"heal_latest_run"|"experiment_config_change"|"metric_config_change"

