---Full experiment representation for the detail, create, and update endpoints.
---
---Extends the shared read-side fields in ``ExperimentBaseSerializer`` with the metric
---definitions (``metrics``/``metrics_secondary``/``saved_metrics``) and the write-side
---fields, and refreshes stale action names while serializing. The list endpoint uses the
---leaner ``ExperimentBasicSerializer`` instead.
---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentOutput
---@field id? number
---@field name? string Name of the experiment.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Description of the experiment hypothesis and expected outcomes.
---@field start_date? string|distilled.Null
---@field end_date? string|distilled.Null
---@field feature_flag_key? string Unique key for the experiment's feature flag. Letters, numbers, hyphens, and underscores only. Search existing flags with the feature-flag-get-all tool first — reuse an existing flag when possible.
---@field feature_flag? posthog.experiments.MinimalFeatureFlag
---@field holdout? posthog.experiments.ExperimentHoldout
---@field holdout_id? number|distilled.Null ID of a holdout group to exclude from the experiment.
---@field exposure_cohort? number|distilled.Null
---@field parameters? posthog.experiments.ExperimentParameters|distilled.Null Experiment parameters JSON. Supported keys include `custom_exposure_filter` and `variant_notes` (free-text notes per variant, keyed by variant key). Flag config (variants, rollout, aggregation, payloads, experience continuity) belongs on the `feature_flag` object; send it there. For backward compatibility, config still sent through these deprecated keys is copied onto the linked flag rather than rejected, and reads project the flag's current config back into this field. Excluded variants live on the top-level `excluded_variants` field, not here.
---@field running_time_calculation? posthog.experiments.ExperimentRunningTimeCalculation|distilled.Null Running-time calculator state: `minimum_detectable_effect`, `recommended_running_time`, `recommended_sample_size`, and `exposure_estimate_config`. Canonical home for these keys, which historically lived in `parameters`.
---@field excluded_variants? posthog.experiments.ExperimentOutputExcludedVariantsList|distilled.Null Variant keys to exclude from metric result calculations. Excluded variants are still served to users but omitted from statistical analysis. The baseline variant and holdout pseudo-variants cannot be excluded. Canonical home for what historically lived in `parameters.excluded_variants`.
---@field secondary_metrics? any
---@field saved_metrics? posthog.experiments.ExperimentOutputSavedMetricsList
---@field saved_metrics_ids? posthog.experiments.ExperimentOutputSavedMetricsIdsList|distilled.Null IDs of shared saved metrics to attach to this experiment. Each item has 'id' (saved metric ID) and 'metadata' with 'type' (primary or secondary).
---@field filters? any
---@field archived? boolean Whether the experiment is archived.
---@field deleted? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field created_by? posthog.experiments.UserBasic|distilled.Null
---@field created_at? string
---@field updated_at? string
---@field type? posthog.experiments.ExperimentTypeEnum|distilled.Null Experiment type: web for frontend UI changes, product for backend/API changes. * `web` - web * `product` - product
---@field exposure_criteria? posthog.experiments.ExperimentApiExposureCriteria|distilled.Null Exposure configuration including filter test accounts and custom exposure events.
---@field metrics? posthog.experiments.ExperimentApiMetricsList|distilled.Null Primary experiment metrics. Each metric must have kind='ExperimentMetric' and a metric_type: 'mean' (set source to an EventsNode with an event name), 'funnel' (set series to an array of EventsNode steps), 'ratio' (set numerator and denominator EventsNode entries), or 'retention' (set start_event and completion_event; pass start_event {"kind": "ExperimentExposureNode"} to start retention from the experiment's exposure event). Use the read-data-schema tool with query kind 'events' to find available events in the project.
---@field metrics_secondary? posthog.experiments.ExperimentApiMetricsList|distilled.Null Secondary metrics for additional measurements. Same format as primary metrics.
---@field stats_config? any
---@field scheduling_config? any
---@field conclusion? posthog.experiments.ConclusionEnum|distilled.Null Experiment conclusion: won, lost, inconclusive, stopped_early, or invalid. * `won` - won * `lost` - lost * `inconclusive` - inconclusive * `stopped_early` - stopped_early * `invalid` - invalid
---@field conclusion_comment? string|distilled.Null Comment about the experiment conclusion.
---@field flag_cleanup_task_id? string|distilled.Null ID of the Desktop task opened to remove the experiment's feature-flag code, when one was requested via open_cleanup_pr on end/ship_variant. Read its status via the flag_cleanup_task action.
---@field repository? string|distilled.Null GitHub repository holding this experiment's feature-flag code, in `organization/repository` format. Used as the target of the flag-cleanup pull request opened via open_cleanup_pr on end/ship_variant. When not set, cleanup targets the team's only connected repository and is skipped if the team has several.
---@field primary_metrics_ordered_uuids? posthog.experiments.ExperimentOutputPrimaryMetricsOrderedUuidsList|distilled.Null Display order of the primary metrics, as metric uuids. This is a display hint only: a metric not in the list renders after the listed ones in stored order, and an entry that matches no metric is ignored. Send it only to reorder metrics. Adding or removing metrics does not need it.
---@field secondary_metrics_ordered_uuids? posthog.experiments.ExperimentOutputSecondaryMetricsOrderedUuidsList|distilled.Null Display order of the secondary metrics, as metric uuids. This is a display hint only: a metric not in the list renders after the listed ones in stored order, and an entry that matches no metric is ignored. Send it only to reorder metrics. Adding or removing metrics does not need it.
---@field only_count_matured_users? boolean
---@field version? number|distilled.Null Optimistic-concurrency token. Reads return the experiment's current version, bumped on every update. Send the version you last read with an update to detect concurrent edits: a stale update merges concurrent changes where safe — metric collections per metric uuid, other fields per field — using the base values sent in `original_experiment`, and fails with HTTP 409 only when the same metric or field changed on both sides (or no base value was sent for a changed field). Omit to skip the check.
---@field status? posthog.experiments.ExperimentStatusEnum Experiment lifecycle state: 'draft' (not yet launched), 'running' (launched with active feature flag), 'paused' (running with feature flag deactivated — virtual state derived from feature_flag.active, not stored), 'exposure_frozen' (running with enrollment frozen to the already-exposed cohort while metrics keep flowing — virtual state derived from the flag's release groups, not stored), 'stopped' (ended).
---@field is_legacy? boolean Whether the experiment uses any legacy-engine metrics (ExperimentTrendsQuery or ExperimentFunnelsQuery). Used to flag legacy experiments and gate actions that don't support them, such as duplicate and copy-to-project.
---@field can_freeze_exposure? boolean Whether enrollment can be frozen right now: the experiment must be running (not draft, paused, stopped, or already frozen) and its feature flag must have release conditions that a person cohort can narrow (no group aggregation, no holdout, no early access conditions).
---@field resolved_exposure_event? string The event exposures are actually counted on when the experiment doesn't configure a custom one — `$feature_flag_called`, or `$experiment_exposure` once the team is in the rollout and the experiment started at or after the cutoff. Resolved server-side so clients display the same event the results queries read. For a draft, this is what the experiment would resolve to if launched now.
---@field health posthog.experiments.ExperimentHealth|distilled.Null Always null. Read the health findings from `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/experiments/{id}/health/`: problems in this experiment's configuration and its feature flag that keep it from producing trustworthy results, each with a fix.
---@field user_access_level? string|distilled.Null The effective access level the user has for this object
---@field tags? posthog.experiments.ExperimentOutputTagsList Organizational tags for this experiment (up to 100, 255 characters each).

