---One experiment metric with at least one matching event in a session recording.
---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentSessionMetricHit
---@field metric_uuid string UUID of the experiment metric (inline primary/secondary or saved) whose events fired.
---@field metric_name string Display name of the metric, or an event-derived title (matching the experiment UI) when unnamed.
---@field event_count number Total number of events in the session matching any of the metric's event/action sources.
---@field first_timestamp string Timestamp of the first event in the session matching the metric.
---@field timestamps posthog.experiments.ExperimentSessionMetricHitTimestampsList Ascending timestamps of the metric's matching events in the session, capped at the first 50. event_count is the true total, so this list may be shorter — treat these as seek points, not a count.
---@field sources posthog.experiments.ExperimentSessionMetricHitSourcesList Which of the metric's sources fired, so a hit reads as 'step 2 of 3' or 'the start event of a retention metric' rather than an unqualified 'this metric happened'. Sources with no matching event are omitted, as is the whole breakdown for metrics beyond the scan's aggregate ceiling. A retention metric whose start and completion are the same event contributes only the start source: the completion would match the identical events and render a duplicate.

---Which of the metric's sources fired, so a hit reads as 'step 2 of 3' or 'the start event of a retention metric' rather than an unqualified 'this metric happened'. Sources with no matching event are omitted, as is the whole breakdown for metrics beyond the scan's aggregate ceiling. A retention metric whose start and completion are the same event contributes only the start source: the completion would match the identical events and render a duplicate.
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentSessionMetricHitSourcesList posthog.experiments.ExperimentSessionMetricSourceHit[]

---Ascending timestamps of the metric's matching events in the session, capped at the first 50. event_count is the true total, so this list may be shorter — treat these as seek points, not a count.
