---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentSetupCandidateMetric
---@field window_days number Days of events read, ending now.
---@field source_event string The metric event that was counted.
---@field metric_properties posthog.experiments.ExperimentSetupPropertyFilterList The property filters that were applied to the metric event. Empty when none were passed.
---@field target_event string|distilled.Null The target event the baseline starts from, or null when none was passed.
---@field computed_at string When the numbers were computed. They are cached for an hour.
---@field test_accounts_filtered boolean Whether test accounts were left out. It follows the default a new experiment gets, so the baseline matches the population that experiment analyzes. False when the project defines no test-account filters.
---@field persons_reached number|distilled.Null Persons who sent the target event. Null without target_event.
---@field persons_converted number|distilled.Null Persons who sent the metric event at or after their first target event. Null without target_event.
---@field conversion_rate number|distilled.Null persons_converted divided by persons_reached. Null without target_event.
---@field funnel_baseline_stats posthog.experiments.ExperimentSetupFunnelBaseline|distilled.Null Pass as baseline_stats to experiment-calculate-running-time with metric_type 'funnel'. Null without target_event.
---@field mean_count_baseline_stats posthog.experiments.ExperimentSetupMeanCountBaseline|distilled.Null Pass as baseline_stats to experiment-calculate-running-time with metric_type 'mean_count'. It counts metric events in the whole window, not only after the first target event, so it can overstate the baseline. Null without target_event.
---@field note string|distilled.Null What the mean count baseline counts.
---@field event_volume number|distilled.Null Metric events in the window, with metric_properties applied. 0 means the event did not occur under those filters, so check the event name before you trust a conversion_rate of 0.
---@field unique_persons number|distilled.Null Persons who sent the metric event, with metric_properties applied.

---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentSetupCandidateMetricSection
---@field status posthog.experiments.SetupContextSectionStatusEnum 'ok' when data holds the section. 'skipped' when an input the section needs was not passed. 'timed_out' when the query was too expensive to finish. 'error' when the read failed. Every status other than 'ok' leaves data null, and the other sections are still valid. * `ok` - Ok * `skipped` - Skipped * `timed_out` - Timed Out * `error` - Error
---@field data posthog.experiments.ExperimentSetupCandidateMetric|distilled.Null Baseline of the candidate metric. Skipped without metric_event.

