---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentWatchCardHighlightsList posthog.experiments.ExperimentWatchHighlight[]

---* `behavior` - behavior
---* `friction` - friction
---* `variant_only` - variant_only
---* `metric` - metric
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentWatchCardKindEnum "behavior"|"friction"|"variant_only"|"metric"

---The recordings themselves, most recent first, ready to hand to the recordings list as-is.
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentWatchCardSessionIdsList string[]

---* `only` - only
---* `far_more` - far_more
---* `more` - more
---* `slightly_more` - slightly_more
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentWatchCardStrengthEnum "only"|"far_more"|"more"|"slightly_more"

---* `too_early` - too_early
---* `no_separation` - no_separation
---* `no_recordings` - no_recordings
---* `no_session_linked_exposures` - no_session_linked_exposures
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentWatchEmptyReasonEnum "too_early"|"no_separation"|"no_recordings"|"no_session_linked_exposures"

---One recording a card names first, and the phrase that says why.
---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentWatchHighlight
---@field session_id string The recording to open. Always one of the card's own session_ids.
---@field reason string Everything this recording carries that earned it the place, ready to render as-is, for example '6 rage clicks, 6 errors' or '1 error, did this 4 times'. Every signal the session shows is listed, so the phrase is the whole picture rather than the single strongest part of it. Friction counts run from the moment the person was exposed to the end of the session, so friction before they met the variant is left out; 'did this N times' counts the card's own event. Not a comparison and not a reason the card exists.

---* `exclude` - exclude
---* `first_seen` - first_seen
---@alias posthog.experiments.ExperimentWatchMultipleVariantHandlingEnum "exclude"|"first_seen"

---One variant's compared population.
---@class posthog.experiments.ExperimentWatchVariant
---@field key string The variant key.
---@field persons number Exposed people the comparison read for this variant: the most recently exposed people, each read from their first session after being exposed. Someone selected who had no session in that horizon is not counted here, so this sits at or below the variant's enrollment between date_from and date_to. People rather than sessions because a variant can change how often the flag is evaluated again later, which moves a variant's session count without anyone behaving differently. One session each, from the moment of exposure on, so every variant gets the same amount of behavior per person.
---@field sessions number Sessions those people had within 24 hours of being exposed, and before the experiment ended or this request was made, which is more than the comparison reads: it says how much recorded material sits behind the variant.

