---Raw control-group statistics the calculator uses to derive a baseline value and variance.
---
---Supply this when you want the server to compute the baseline value and (for ratio/retention)
---the delta-method variance, instead of passing `baseline_value`/`variance` directly.
---@class posthog.experiments.RunningTimeBaselineStats
---@field number_of_samples number Number of control-group samples (users/units) observed.
---@field sum number Sum of the metric values across the control group (for funnels, the numerator/conversions).
---@field sum_squares? number Sum of squared metric values. Mean metrics read their variance from it, and ratio/retention metrics need it. Without it, a mean metric's variance is approximated from the baseline value.
---@field denominator_sum? number|distilled.Null Sum of the denominator values. Required for ratio/retention metrics.
---@field denominator_sum_squares? number|distilled.Null Sum of squared denominator values (ratio/retention variance).
---@field numerator_denominator_sum_product? number|distilled.Null Sum of numerator×denominator products, used for the delta-method covariance term.
---@field step_counts? posthog.experiments.RunningTimeBaselineStatsStepCountsList Per-step counts for funnel metrics; the last entry is the final-step count.

---Per-step counts for funnel metrics; the last entry is the final-step count.
---@alias posthog.experiments.RunningTimeBaselineStatsStepCountsList number[]

---Estimated sample size and running time for the given inputs.
---@class posthog.experiments.RunningTimeCalculationResult
---@field baseline_value number|distilled.Null Baseline metric value used in the calculation (echoed or derived from stats).
---@field variance number|distilled.Null Variance used in the calculation; null for funnel metrics (implicit in p(1-p)).
---@field recommended_sample_size number|distilled.Null Total recommended sample size across all variants. Null if inputs are insufficient.
---@field recommended_running_time_days number|distilled.Null Estimated days to reach the recommended sample size. Null when exposure_rate_per_day is omitted.

---What the experiment can detect over time, at its exposure rate so far.
---@class posthog.experiments.RunningTimeOutlook
---@field days_since_launch number Days since the experiment launched, with fractions.
---@field exposures_per_day number Exposures that count toward the target, per day from launch to the end of the window the current results cover.
---@field detectable_effect_now number The smallest relative change, as a percentage, that the exposures so far can detect.
---@field upcoming_checkpoints posthog.experiments.RunningTimeOutlookUpcomingCheckpointsList Up to three week marks after today, out of weeks 1, 2, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 26 and 52, with the change each can detect at the exposure rate so far.
---@field reachable_effect number The smallest relative change, as a percentage, that the experiment can detect within four weeks from today. A target for a smaller change is out of reach.

---Up to three week marks after today, out of weeks 1, 2, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 26 and 52, with the change each can detect at the exposure rate so far.
---@alias posthog.experiments.RunningTimeOutlookUpcomingCheckpointsList posthog.experiments.DetectableEffectCheckpoint[]

---The target sample of the experiment's running time estimate.
---@class posthog.experiments.RunningTimeTarget
---@field minimum_detectable_effect number The relative change, as a percentage, that the target sample is sized to detect.
---@field recommended_sample_size number|distilled.Null Exposures needed across the analyzed variants, so that the comparison of each variant with the control can detect the minimum detectable effect at the analysis's confidence level and 80% power. In manual running time mode, the saved target. Otherwise sized from the first primary metric's current result, with the variance the analysis uses and the flag's traffic split. Null when no result can size it yet. The variances come from the result and don't depend on the effect, so the sample scales with 1 / effect²: the target for another effect is recommended_sample_size × (minimum_detectable_effect / effect)².
---@field current_sample_size number|distilled.Null Exposures so far that count toward the target: the control's and those of the variants that get traffic. A variant at 0% does not count. Null in manual mode, and when no result can size the target.
---@field outlook posthog.experiments.RunningTimeOutlook|distilled.Null What the experiment can detect over time, on the same curve the target is sized on. Null in manual mode, before launch, when the current results cover less than 0.1 days, and when no result can size the target.

